<section class="page-header">
  <a class="back-link" href="/training">← Back to Training</a>
  <h1 class="h1"><%= mod.title %></h1>
  <div class="sub"><%= mod.subtitle %> · <%= mod.minutes %> min</div>
</section>

<% if (completed) { %>
  <div class="completion-banner">
    <span class="completion-icon">✓</span>
    <div>
      <div class="completion-title">Module 5 Complete</div>
      <div class="completion-sub">Your progress has been recorded. You can review the material any time.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
<% } %>

<article class="card lesson">
  <h2 class="lesson-h">Federal Protected Classes Under the Fair Housing Act</h2>
  <ul class="lesson-list">
    <li>Race</li>
    <li>Color</li>
    <li>National Origin</li>
    <li>Religion</li>
    <li>Sex <span class="muted">(including gender identity and sexual orientation per HUD 2021)</span></li>
    <li>Familial Status</li>
    <li>Disability</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">Pennsylvania Additions</h2>
  <ul class="lesson-list">
    <li>Age (40 and over)</li>
    <li>Ancestry</li>
    <li>Use of guide or support animal</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">Ohio Additions</h2>
  <ul class="lesson-list">
    <li>Ancestry</li>
    <li>Military status</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">What Steering Looks Like</h2>
  <p>
    Steering is directing a buyer or renter toward or away from a particular neighborhood, building,
    or property based on protected class. Examples:
  </p>
  <ul class="lesson-list">
    <li>"This neighborhood might not be a good fit for your family" — <em>familial status steering</em></li>
    <li>"Let me show you homes where you'll feel more comfortable" — <em>racial steering</em></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Even well-intentioned suggestions can be steering.</p>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">What Your Advertising Cannot Say</h2>
  <ul class="lesson-list">
    <li>"Great for families" — <em>familial status</em></li>
    <li>"Adults only" — <em>familial status and age (except legal senior housing)</em></li>
    <li>"Christian neighborhood" — <em>religion</em></li>
    <li>"Within walking distance of synagogue" — <em>religion</em></li>
    <li>"No wheelchairs" — <em>disability</em></li>
    <li>"Perfect bachelor pad" — <em>sex / familial status</em></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">Code of Ethics Basics (Article 10)</h2>
  <p>
    REALTORS shall not deny equal professional services to any person for reasons of race, color,
    religion, sex, handicap, familial status, national origin, sexual orientation, or gender identity.
    This applies to listing, showing, financing, and every stage of the transaction.
  </p>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">What To Do If You Witness a Violation</h2>
  <ol class="lesson-ol">
    <li>Document what you observed — date, time, parties, statements made</li>
    <li>Report to your broker immediately</li>
    <li>Do not confront the other party yourself</li>
    <li>Broker escalates to brokerage compliance and state commission as required</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="lesson-h">Dual Agency Rules</h2>
  <p>
    Dual agency is legal in PA and OH with written informed consent from both parties. You must
    disclose in writing before either party signs an agreement. Dual agents owe loyalty to both —
    they cannot advocate for price on either side. Many brokerages prohibit dual agency entirely.
  </p>
</article>

<!-- CONFIRMATION QUESTION -->
<section class="card quiz-card" id="quiz">
  <h2 class="h2">Confirmation Question</h2>
  <p class="quiz-prompt">
    Ohio adds which protected class beyond the federal Fair Housing Act protected classes?
  </p>

  <form action="/training/module/5/submit" method="POST" id="quiz-form">
    <% const opts = [
      { v: 'A', t: 'Age' },
      { v: 'B', t: 'Military status' },
      { v: 'C', t: 'Ancestry' },
      { v: 'D', t: 'Sexual orientation' }
    ]; %>
    <% opts.forEach(o => { %>
      <label class="quiz-option">
        <input type="radio" name="answer" value="<%= o.v %>" <%= completed ? 'disabled' : '' %> />
        <span class="quiz-letter"><%= o.v %></span>
        <span><%= o.t %></span>
      </label>
    <% }); %>

    <% if (result === 'correct') { %>
      <div class="quiz-result correct">
        <span class="check">✓</span> Correct! Module 5 Complete.
      </div>
    <% } else if (result === 'incorrect') { %>
      <div class="quiz-result incorrect">
        Incorrect. Review the module and try again.
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <% if (!completed) { %>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-block">Submit Answer</button>
    <% } else { %>
      <a href="/training" class="btn btn-primary btn-block">Back to Training</a>
    <% } %>
  </form>
</section>
